<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mohammad Mosaddegh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1882–1967</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mohammad Mosaddegh was an Iranian nationalist who served as prime minister from 1951 to 1953. He led the nationalisation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bp">Anglo-Iranian Oil Company</a> in 1951, provoking a British boycott of Iranian oil. In August 1953 he was overthrown in a coup backed by the CIA and MI6 that restored the power of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammad-reza-pahlavi">Mohammad Reza Shah</a>, and he spent his last years under house arrest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mohammad-mosaddegh.jpg" alt="Mohammad Mosaddegh" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: International News Photos · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dr_Mohammad_Mosaddeq.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
